453:   /**
454:    * Executes the given action with the promise value, on a blocking thread.
455:    * <p>
456:    * Similar to {@link #blockingMap(Function)}, but does not provide a new value.
457:    * This can be used to do something with the value, without terminating the promise.
458:    *
459:    * @param action the action to to perform with the value, on a blocking thread
460:    * @return a promise for the same value given to the action
461:    */
462:   default Promise<T> blockingOp(Action<? super T> action) {
463:     return flatMap(t -> Blocking.op(action.curry(t)).map(() -> t));
464:   }
